stateDiagram-v2
    state "No failure key" as absent
    state "1 to 4 failures; fixed deadline" as available
    state "5 failures; same deadline" as exhausted
    [*] --> absent
    absent --> available: first admissible wrong OTP / SET 1 EX 900
    available --> available: wrong OTP below fifth / INCR preserves deadline
    available --> exhausted: fifth wrong OTP / INCR to 5
    absent --> absent: correct OTP / no write
    available --> available: correct OTP / no reset or deadline change
    exhausted --> exhausted: any OTP / refuse without write
    available --> absent: native Valkey expiry
    exhausted --> absent: native Valkey expiry
    note right of exhausted
        App/com signup and email sign-in; app/com/org destination confirmation.
        EmailOtpVerificationFailureBudget and TelephoneOtpVerificationFailureBudget own separate policies.
        Sharing here means candidate/flow/browser reuse within the explicit scope, not channel policy sharing.
        Existing recovery/reentry callers use their own purpose scopes.
        Dummy email sign-in counts well-formed attempts and cannot succeed.
        Key scope: surface, purpose, channel, normalized destination digest.
        Candidate, flow, browser and owner do not partition the budget.
        Candidate lock and OTP expiry remain independent controls.
        Corruption or dependency failure raises; verification cannot consume OTP.
        Same-scope third-party exhaustion can deny verification for at most 15 minutes.
